    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox[
       TemplateBox[{
        "\"Four warp-bubble shape functions f(r) sharing the same boundary \
conditions f(0) = 1, f(\[Infinity]) = 0.  Tanh is the original Alcubierre \
profile; the others differ only in how sharply the wall falls off and whether \
the support is compact (CompactPolynomial, SmoothStep) or asymptotic (Tanh, \
Gaussian).\""},
        "RowDefault"],
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->720]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{20, 20}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"4494c0d2-2be0-4ccf-b894-98a4e414990d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each profile satisfies the same boundary conditions \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"f", "(", "0", ")", "=", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "083d8bac-2774-423c-86be-5a48e9b683ad"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"f", "(", "\[Infinity]", ")", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "72f9e066-15c4-44c8-86be-42e87cace220"],
 " \[LongDash] but they differ in how sharp the wall is and whether the \
support is compact.  Sharper walls localise the exotic matter into a thinner \
shell at the cost of larger derivatives, which means more curvature, which \
means more energy.  This is the first hint that the energy bill of a warp \
drive is essentially set by the ",
 StyleBox["geometry of the wall",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", not by the bubble's velocity."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9f3bf7bc-0815-4c95-b530-5149a681a9b8"],

Cell["2. The metric in ADM form", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"794af66b-3ce2-43a6-b701-2a442bc871e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every warp drive in the literature is most natural in the 3+1 ADM \
formulation.  Foliate spacetime into spatial slices labelled by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["t", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "2690b376-01c4-4bc2-8604-4d2817a9af34"],
 "; on each slice keep the spatial metric ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
    RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "b83311db-b890-49ff-86c6-120a2e679f99"],
 "; relate proper time on neighbouring slices by the lapse ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Alpha]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "7db84026-bd42-4458-8634-e66f0eb45646"],
 "; relate spatial coordinates between slices by the shift vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "4b295625-2bba-496a-b6cc-22235f3dbbbf"],
 ".  The line element splits into a temporal-distance piece and a \
spatial-displacement piece:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"40e182b3-e835-40fb-a9d5-d7a0156e0afc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["ds", "2"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "2"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["dt", "2"]}], "+", 
   SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
    RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["dx", "i"], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], "dt"}]}], ")"}], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["dx", "j"], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "j"], "dt"}]}], ")"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"0778ec23-5cc5-447c-9736-ef01bc5d0891"],

Cell["\<\
Reading off matrix entries gives the standard 3+1 decomposition of the \
4-metric:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e01d7bf0-8e59-4c09-96b0-bf2c2df08d74"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["g", "00"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "2"], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",\

 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"c1692428-bfb7-4b11-968a-ab21a2bb66ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["g", 
    RowBox[{"0", "i"}]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "j"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"12590601-c201-405f-92ec-41dd3079619b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["g", "ij"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
    RowBox[{"i", "j"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"f6b0a2b2-b8d1-448c-986f-1bbc780001fb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with summation convention on the spatial indices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"i", ",", "j", "\[Element]", 
    RowBox[{"{", "1", ",", "2", ",", "3", "}"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "1efa0293-a414-4941-b8b4-3e652b66ed19"],
 " and the spatial-metric raise/lower ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "j"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "ef132895-a6a4-417c-91e0-ff6bf15472e6"],
 ".  The inverse 4-metric has a similarly clean form: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["g", "00"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
      RowBox[{"-", "2"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "358dfc67-76a6-4cca-a720-dc88883b5761"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["g", 
     RowBox[{"0", "i"}]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
      RowBox[{"-", "2"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "5faea3c0-69c6-41d5-8313-fb6fc10e5010"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["g", "ij"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "j"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
      RowBox[{"-", "2"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "c2d51e25-8931-4bea-93a1-cddde811243a"],
 ", which is exactly what ",
 StyleBox["ADMInverse[\[Alpha], \[Beta], \[Gamma]]", "Input"],
 " in the package returns."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6a50d28a-cf09-432e-8d68-eaff53adea03"],

Cell["\<\
For Alcubierre's drive the ADM ingredients are spectacularly simple:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"669b8a3c-9956-4c56-911b-bfff553b3530"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", 
      SubscriptBox["v", "s"], " ", 
      RowBox[{"f", "(", 
       SubscriptBox["r", "s"], ")"}]}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], ")"}],
    ",", "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "=", "1"}], ",", "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], "=", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"8608f6bc-ae28-484d-b099-a667b383f12e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All the warp \"weirdness\" lives in that single ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "554caf63-a92c-4478-937a-ad56c425dac6"],
 " term \[LongDash] a unit-magnitude vector field along the direction of \
motion, modulated by the shape function so it switches on inside the bubble \
and off outside.  In Wolfram, the helper ",
 StyleBox["AlcubierreMetric", "Input"],
 " builds the full 4-metric symbolically:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"93ab0662-d847-42e7-adc8-36761ab40ae4"],

Cell["\<\
g = AlcubierreMetric[{1, 1, 8}, {t, x, y, z}];   (* {v0, R, \[Sigma]} *)
MatrixForm @ g\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"dfbd38d2-fb5f-4049-9898-00c37e87a0e9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "=", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "c4e412b2-bad4-4cd8-844a-aaab3d3a1bed"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"det", "(", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}]], ")", "=", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "00e92868-d1fd-4431-a05c-9516928850c4"],
 " the formula above gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"det", "(", 
    SubscriptBox["g", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], ")", "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "2160c2af-2805-4cb1-8099-7719b13650d1"],
 " everywhere, and Wolfram simplifies ",
 StyleBox["Det[g]", "Input"],
 " back to that exact value:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ca4b342f-4e1b-4d40-94b4-0fd4951d01de"],

Cell["\<\
Simplify @ Det @ AlcubierreMetric[{v, R, s}, {t, x, y, z}]
(* -> -1 *)\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"a1f53a25-121e-485d-9c4d-9a40b5129287"],

Cell["3. Einstein tensor in three lines", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1f6dace1-57aa-407f-b597-9153ff14c7b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is where Wolfram earns its keep.  In the Python port we built \
finite-difference Christoffel symbols, then finite-difference Riemann \
tensors, then finite-difference Ricci, all ~500 lines.  In Wolfram the \
equivalent is a literal transliteration of the textbook formula because ",
 StyleBox["D", "Input"],
 " differentiates symbolically.  Recall the Christoffel symbols of the second \
kind:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5a043f99-a7f4-45df-a782-b3d7ff533d2e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Mu]"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "2"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["g", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Alpha]"], " ", 
       SubscriptBox["g", 
        RowBox[{"\[Beta]", "\[Nu]"}]]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Beta]"], " ", 
       SubscriptBox["g", 
        RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Nu]"}]]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Nu]"], " ", 
       SubscriptBox["g", 
        RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}]]}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"d29e3679-74de-47c5-a3ff-0cc1d03043c1"],

Cell["In Wolfram this is one Table loop:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbbf8176-95d8-410d-9f0b-a318180bf7c7"],

Cell["\<\
ChristoffelSymbols[g_, {t_, x_, y_, z_}] := Module[
  {ginv = Inverse[g],
   dg = Table[D[g, c], {c, {t, x, y, z}}]},
  Table[
    (1/2) Sum[ginv[[m, n]] (dg[[a, b, n]] + dg[[b, a, n]] - dg[[n, a, b]]),
              {n, 4}],
    {m, 4}, {a, 4}, {b, 4}]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"606c44c8-579b-44b0-8867-ee198bba55d9"],

Cell["\<\
The Riemann tensor follows from the standard non-commutativity of covariant \
derivatives,\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a8969abf-4a25-438a-978a-7a4ca5296c26"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["R", 
    RowBox[{"\[Sigma]", "\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}], "\[Rho]"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], " ", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "\[Sigma]"}], "\[Rho]"]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Nu]"], " ", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Sigma]"}], "\[Rho]"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Lambda]"}], "\[Rho]"], " ", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "\[Sigma]"}], "\[Lambda]"]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "\[Lambda]"}], "\[Rho]"], " ", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Sigma]"}], "\[Lambda]"]}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"0f2e4158-96cd-433b-b3f8-aa940ef2212e"],

Cell["\<\
and Ricci is a single contraction, the Ricci scalar a second one:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"557aa83d-ea55-4d99-b1a0-f5c898ccc40e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["R", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["R", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Rho]", "\[Nu]"}], "\[Rho]"], ",", 
   "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{"R", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["g", 
      RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], " ", 
     SubscriptBox["R", 
      RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"3d4c92c0-86fe-4e44-8c5c-693b3d9f76eb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "8f1cefe9-b582-45a4-ac5a-2bbf415ee31b"],
 " denoting partial differentiation with respect to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "c0fc17a5-332b-4145-8eb9-9c87b9d79cd6"],
 " and the usual Einstein summation convention.  The Einstein tensor is then \
a one-line definition:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"db154801-3075-400f-adcd-33764a1ffe49"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["G", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["R", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["1", "2"], " ", 
     SubscriptBox["g", 
      RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], " ", "R"}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"67ced984-6318-4912-a85b-f319e73f278a"],

Cell["Through the field equation", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c644ef8c-2867-4d21-b864-ee38fb69a87c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["G", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], "=", 
   RowBox[{"8", "\[Pi]", " ", 
    SubscriptBox["T", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"be79182c-a156-4aea-8bdd-d885ab2f94b6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"G", "=", "c", "=", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "e0901486-23d3-43dd-bd71-b5b6e91ba3f7"],
 ", we read off the matter content the metric implies:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d1c3aa99-3502-49cf-9ba7-d0b629b00a98"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["T", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox["G", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], 
    RowBox[{"8", "\[Pi]"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"c295f272-8c7a-4e48-bf20-81b87550e190"],

Cell["\<\
In Wolfram that's a one-liner.  At a point on the bubble wall:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07c08039-eaf2-4c47-a869-c652bdbf889c"],

Cell["\<\
GAt = EinsteinTensor[g, {t, x, y, z}] /.
       {t -> 0, x -> 1.0, y -> 0.2, z -> 0};
N @ Chop @ GAt // MatrixForm
(*  GAt[[1,1]] = 8 Pi T_{00} -- the energy density measured by a
    *static* coordinate observer (4-velocity (1,0,0,0)).  This is
    NOT the Eulerian-observer energy density rho_Eulerian =
    T_{mu nu} n^mu n^nu, which is contracted with the unit normal
    n = (1, -beta^i)/alpha and is computed by EulerianEnergyDensity.
    The (0,i) entries are momentum density components and the
    ij-block is anisotropic stress.  *)\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"ab041255-6f55-4694-978c-1d436a001deb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For Alcubierre the energy density seen by an Eulerian (slice-normal) \
observer admits a famous closed form, derived by Alcubierre in the original \
paper (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox["z", "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "2b760c27-311e-4587-97dd-0226370300cd"],
 " is the squared transverse distance from the bubble's direction-of-motion \
axis):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00f6741a-3e04-47f4-9b6a-55e50344fddd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"\[Rho]", "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    FractionBox[
     SuperscriptBox[
      SubscriptBox["v", "s"], "2"], 
     RowBox[{"32", "\[Pi]"}]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      FractionBox["df", 
       RowBox[{"d", 
        SubscriptBox["r", "s"]}]], ")"}], "2"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["y", "2"], "+", 
      SuperscriptBox["z", "2"]}], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      SubscriptBox["r", "s"], "2"]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"3f4c27e9-22af-4b74-84e1-4ad0f357dc2a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plotted in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"z", "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "4a25de3c-1168-4da7-9948-0889a1abe97d"],
 " plane it's strikingly anisotropic \[LongDash] zero on the \
direction-of-motion axis, peaking in two crescent-shaped regions in the \
bubble wall.  Note the colour scale: the values are ",
 StyleBox["negative everywhere",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " they are non-zero.  This is the punchline of the original 1994 paper:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e5c390ea-ecfd-4e5e-9494-5528547b9fa5"],

Cell["\<\
DensityPlot[
  AlcubierreAnalyticEnergyDensity[{1, 1, 8}, {0, x, y, 0}],
  {x, -2.5, 2.5}, {y, -2.5, 2.5},
  PlotPoints -> 220, ColorFunction -> \"TemperatureMap\",
  PlotLegends -> Automatic,
  Epilog -> {Black, Thick, Circle[{0, 0}, 1]}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"c4bd1ae5-35df-4073-9a14-e87227ce0953"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     GraphicsBox[
      TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["
