      FrameRate -> 8, AnimationRunning -> True, AnimationRepetitions -> 
       DirectedInfinity[1]]]},
    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox[
       TemplateBox[{
        "\"Figure 5. Top-down view of the same scene.  Same metric, same \
bubble velocity, same spacecraft, but no z-axis cosmetics so the geometry is \
unobstructed.  The red crescents are the actual analytic Eulerian \[Rho] \
(more red = more exotic matter required); the cyan grid is the \"", 
         RowBox[{"StyleBox", "[", 
           RowBox[{"\"instantaneous\"", ",", 
             RowBox[{"FontSlant", "\[Rule]", "Italic"}]}], "]"}], 
         "\" coordinate distortion \"", 
         "\"\\!\\(\\*StyleBox[\\\"x\\\", \\\"TI\\\"]\\) \[RightArrow] \
\\!\\(\\*StyleBox[\\\"x\\\", \\\"TI\\\"]\\) + 0.5\\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\\"\
\[Beta]\\\", \\\"x\\\"]\\)(\\!\\(\\*StyleBox[\\\"t\\\", \\\"TI\\\"]\\))\"", 
         "\" \[LongDash] a snapshot of the metric geometry at each frame, \
scaled by 0.5 for visibility \[LongDash] not a Lagrangian-advected mesh, so \
it returns to a flat grid wherever the bubble is far away.  Compare with \
Figure 6 below, which shows the genuinely cumulative displacement of comoving \
test particles.  The dashed white circle is the nominal bubble radius.\""},
        "RowDefault"],
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->720]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{20, 20}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"7e53a5f8-b429-4a49-a5aa-2658481c9a48"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both animations are rendered entirely from the analytic Alcubierre formulas \
\[LongDash] no GR solver, no NDSolve, just the closed forms for the shape \
function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"f", "(", 
    SubscriptBox["r", "s"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "ec7dfb3c-9141-4c3d-b69b-1ce2f7b905fd"],
 ", the shift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "x"], "=", "-", 
    SubscriptBox["v", "s"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     SubscriptBox["r", "s"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "be1512af-67c8-4c55-9f1d-e3a7204263b7"],
 ", and the Eulerian energy density.  Both run in seconds.  The spacecraft \
mesh and animation logic add fewer than 200 lines of Wolfram on top of the \
existing package."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"52312f50-084a-4f2a-844c-cd1ffe436507"],

Cell["6. The grid being warped", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5ab1b0eb-49c5-4db5-9056-08432736b3bb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Another way to see what the bubble is doing to the geometry is to drop a \
regular Cartesian grid into the spacetime and let the shift field advect \
every grid intersection.  As the bubble sweeps from left to right across the \
frame the grid lines locally bunch up in front of it and stretch out behind \
it.  The animation below uses a 15\[Times]15 grid, the analytic Alcubierre \
shift field with v=c and R=1, and a simple Euler advection step following the \
Eulerian-observer law ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"d", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "i"], "/", "dt"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "b00255ae-b51b-4bee-8315-40cc4a62df48"],
 "=",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "4adc22f5-210b-4fb0-a795-3a447d4b742d"],
 "=",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["v", "s"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     SubscriptBox["r", "s"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "b3d22384-798d-4f74-9dc6-eced334276d1"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1f2f89a9-accb-404b-b80b-be687d1da6d0"],

Cell["\<\
alcShift[t_, x_, y_] := +1.0 TanhShape[Sqrt[(x - 1.0 t)^2 + y^2], 1, 8];
(* alcShift returns +v_s f = -beta^x = Eulerian 3-velocity. *)

advect[{x0_, y0_}, t_, nstep_] := Module[{x = x0, y = y0, dt = t/nstep},
  Do[{x, y} = {x + dt alcShift[k dt, x, y], y}, {k, 0, nstep - 1}];
  {x, y}];

frame[t_] := Show[
  DensityPlot[
    AlcubierreExpansionScalar[{1, 1, 8}, {t, x, y, 0}],
    {x, -3, 3}, {y, -2.5, 2.5},
    ColorFunction -> \"RedBlueTones\", Frame -> True,
    PlotLegends -> Automatic],
  Graphics[{Thickness[0.0015], Black,
    Table[Line[Table[advect[{x, yi}, t, 14], {x, -3, 3, 6/60}]],
          {yi, -3, 3, 6/14}],
    Table[Line[Table[advect[{xi, y}, t, 14], {y, -3, 3, 6/60}]],
          {xi, -3, 3, 6/14}]}]];
ListAnimate[Table[frame[t], {t, 0, 2, 2/29.}]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"759d42a3-0f23-4761-8cf8-c9758615dcce"],

