       DirectedInfinity[1]]]},
    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox[
       TemplateBox[{"\"Figure 6. A regular Cartesian grid \"", 
         RowBox[{"StyleBox", "[", 
           RowBox[{"\"cumulatively\"", ",", 
             RowBox[{"FontSlant", "\[Rule]", "Italic"}]}], "]"}], 
         "\" advected by the Alcubierre shift field as the bubble sweeps from \
left to right.  Each grid intersection is a comoving test particle: once the \
bubble has pushed it, it stays at its new position because the shift field \
provides no restoring force \[LongDash] this is why the grid stays deformed \
behind the bubble, in contrast to the \"", 
         RowBox[{"StyleBox", "[", 
           RowBox[{"\"instantaneous\"", ",", 
             RowBox[{"FontSlant", "\[Rule]", "Italic"}]}], "]"}], 
         "\" coordinate-distortion mesh in Figure 5.  The background colour \
is the Eulerian expansion scalar \[Theta] (red = contraction in front of the \
bubble, blue = expansion behind).  Inside the bubble all four points of any \
small grid cell move together \[LongDash] no internal stretching, no tidal \
forces.  All the deformation is concentrated in the wall.\""},
        "RowDefault"],
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->720]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{20, 20}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"726083c7-4d70-4e32-bb4a-de9ef03af982"],

Cell["7. Geodesics: getting swept up by a warp bubble", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1b68ee98-dc4d-4e83-9490-48b28f2d1b8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Drop a population of test particles into the spacetime and let them follow \
geodesics.  Free-fall trajectories ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"], "(", "\[Lambda]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "3b5daec8-61bf-4278-9617-419de1a9fadc"],
 " obey the geodesic equation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cafa7e20-7979-4858-bb40-95c492d0d29c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["d", "2"], 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"]}], 
    RowBox[{"d", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "2"]}]], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Mu]"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Alpha]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Beta]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"]}], "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"834ed910-5afb-409c-b53c-ae0cb5d8dd75"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "which we rewrite as a first-order ODE system for position and 4-velocity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"d", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"], "/", "d\[Lambda]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "84d0445f-004b-48ca-b604-b0398f9bcc8d"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8b2bebb2-c7dc-4d5a-a4cd-871b0e89a9fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"]}], ",", 
   "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Mu]"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Alpha]"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Beta]"]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",\

 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"8660cd6a-c83a-4cad-b213-16afc127a0b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For massive (timelike) particles the affine parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Lambda]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "782b4562-34c5-46eb-a77f-0230d297301b"],
 " can be chosen to be the proper time, and the velocity is normalised so that"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8e9c87a4-2634-44df-911f-6d9c61274be4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["g", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Nu]"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"ef612d0f-066c-4529-a1ec-64335da41e7c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For light rays (null geodesics) the normalisation becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["g", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["k", "\[Mu]"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["k", "\[Nu]"], "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "1301090e-f71d-4b5b-a2b9-6da78550f8f5"],
 " instead, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Lambda]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "4393e011-b3c0-4936-9037-0260e2c2539b"],
 " is no longer proper time (which is zero for a photon) but any affine \
parameter along the ray.  The Christoffel coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "31824d88-3ef3-45dd-ba5d-f8b507590fbe"],
 " in the right-hand side are the same expressions Wolfram generated \
symbolically in Section 3 \[LongDash] we just substitute the current ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "567574c5-a9e6-4bac-8bb7-c05b086d17b9"],
 " values into them and hand the result to ",
 StyleBox["NDSolve", "Input"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4cd7676c-b234-4a62-8714-a1c3e61268fc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In ADM language an Eulerian observer (the analogue of a stationary one in \
flat space) has spatial 3-velocity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "aad5acb9-0462-4cf5-a073-05d042ff7790"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["v", "s"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     SubscriptBox["r", "s"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "ed4b74a5-f279-4270-8523-8b154f26d9af"],
 " (positive, forward).  We place eight initially stationary particles ahead \
of the bubble; as the bubble overtakes them from behind, each one is grabbed \
by the shift field and dragged forward.  Particles on the bubble axis get the \
deepest grip; particles further off-axis are partly missed by the wall and \
feel proportionally less drag:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f4c200f-ed3e-4449-9a23-0c123b91c570"],

Cell["\<\
alcShift[t_, x_, y_] := +1.0 TanhShape[Sqrt[(x - 1.0 t)^2 + y^2], 1, 8];

(* Eulerian-observer advection: dx/dt = -beta^x = +v_s f(r_s).
   alcShift here returns the magnitude +v_s f, which is exactly
   -beta^x for an Alcubierre bubble.  Use a fixed Euler step. *)
sweep[{x0_, y0_}, ts_] := With[{dt = ts[[2]] - ts[[1]]},
  FoldList[
    {#1[[1]] + dt alcShift[#2, #1[[1]], y0], #1[[2]]} &,
    {x0, y0}, Rest[ts]]];

ts = Range[0., 4., 0.05];
trajs = Table[sweep[{2., y0}, ts], {y0, Range[-1.4, 1.4, 0.35]}];
ListAnimate @ Table[
  Show[DensityPlot[
         AlcubierreExpansionScalar[{1, 1, 8}, {ts[[k]], x, y, 0}],
         {x, -1, 6}, {y, -2, 2}, PlotPoints -> 90,
         ColorFunction -> \"RedBlueTones\", PlotLegends -> Automatic],
       Graphics[{Black, Thick, Line /@ (Take[#, k] & /@ trajs),
         Red, PointSize[0.022], Point /@ (#[[k]] & /@ trajs)}]],
  {k, 1, Length[ts], 2}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"a0376680-5fc4-4d57-bf88-6f2934cd5b0f"],

